   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Elenga-Hatikamrul-Rangpur Road of the Dhaka-Northwest international trade corridor upgraded 
Indicator: 190 km of road upgraded with climate-resilient design (2016 baseline: 0 km) 
Achievement: 150 
Progress/Status: Eleven contracts (WP-05 to WP-15) have been awarded. As of 31 December 2025, the physical progress of these11 packages are WP-5:34.25% WP-6: 79.48%, WP-7: 87.26%, WP-8: 99.18%, WP-9:99.05%, WP-10: 92.93%, WP-11: 98.88%, WP- 12:99.13%. As of 31 December2025, the overall physical progress was 83.78%.

The Achieved Progress of SASEC-2 (awarded contracts) up to December  2025 was 83.78 %. This delayed progress has been occurred due to less intension of the Contractors, small scaled construction, less procurement of the materials, LA issues, delayed shifting of U/G Utilities, un-demolished obstacles and COVID-19 etc. So, all Contractors have been reminded about the progress behind schedule
 
Data Source: RHD project performance report</narrative>
    </description>
